assessments:
  - discriminant: mcq
    value:
      id: 513-mcq-01
      prompt: A business uses barcode scanners at the warehouse and a web-based dashboard at head office. When stock is scanned, the dashboard updates in real time. This is an example of which principle?
      options:
        - Different parts of a system communicating with each other
        - Offline-first data entry
        - Local-only inventory management
        - Manual stock reconciliation
      correct_index: 0
      feedback_correct: |
        Correct. The barcode scanner (hardware) and the dashboard
        (software on a remote server) are different parts of the
        same system communicating in real time. This is exactly
        what the spec means by "how different parts of the system
        communicate with each other."
      feedback_incorrect: |
        The answer is "different parts of a system communicating
        with each other". The scenario explicitly describes a
        scanner (one part) and a dashboard (another part)
        exchanging data automatically, which is the definition of
        system communication in an automated stock control
        context.
